A high disease-association score does not tell us how a gene should be used therapeutically.
A candidate may be:

a plausible combination target;
a predictive or resistance biomarker;
a tumor-intrinsic driver;
a mechanistic marker with limited direct tractability;
or a biologically relevant but poor direct therapeutic target.

Collapsing these roles into one ranking obscures the translational question.

